{
    "background_story": "Mckenzie was a renowned zoologist who had always been fascinated by the hyrax, a small, mysterious mammal native to Africa and the Middle East. Growing up in South Africa, she spent countless hours observing these creatures in their natural habitat. Her groundbreaking research on the social behavior of hyraxes earned her a prestigious grant to lead an expedition to the Ethiopian Highlands. There, she discovered a previously unknown species of hyrax, which she named 'Procavia mckenziei' in honor of her own family's legacy. Mckenzie's tireless efforts to protect the hyrax and its habitats have made her a leading voice in conservation circles. Her love for these remarkable creatures has inspired a new generation of scientists and wildlife enthusiasts.",
